5. Nrfr, by Ackites and contributors
   https://github.com/Ackites/Nrfr
   Apache-2.0: Nrfr-LICENSE.txt.
   Referenced for the Android CarrierConfig override approach and key names.
   TideCard uses a separately written Java backend, nonpersistent overrides,
   saved restoration snapshots, scoped slot selection and a watchdog.
   The 2.3.0-rc1 compatibility design also references a5533348/Nrfr,
   commit 6c05f224dc802d0df952db93a6d2852a91c9edb0 (Apache-2.0):
   no-restart instrumentation and temporary shell permission delegation.
   TideCard independently implements authenticated completion callbacks,
   fixed three-key nonpersistent writes, and conservative failure handling.
   No fork APK or HiddenApiBypass library is bundled.

